APPLEACCOUNTTRANSPARENCYD(8)                           System Manager's Manual

NAME
     appleaccounttransparencyd – Apple Account Transparency daemon

SYNOPSIS
     appleaccounttransparencyd

DESCRIPTION
     The appleaccounttransparencyd daemon manages Apple Account transparency
     event storage and serves XPC clients via the
     com.apple.appleaccount.transparency Mach service.

     The daemon stores and retrieves transparency events for the current Apple
     Account user, supporting both read-only production clients and privileged
     utility clients.  XPC clients holding the
     com.apple.appleaccount.transparency entitlement may call fetchUserEvents.
     Clients additionally holding the
     com.apple.appleaccount.transparency.utility entitlement may perform the
     full set of CRUD and lifecycle operations.

     appleaccounttransparencyd is launched on-demand by launchd(8) and must
     not be invoked directly by users or processes; all interaction must occur
     through the designated XPC service name.

FILES
     /System/Library/LaunchAgents/com.apple.appleaccounttransparencyd.plist
             The launchd(8) property list that registers the daemon on macOS.

     /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks/AppleAccountTransparency.framework/Versions/A/appleaccounttransparencyd
             The daemon executable on macOS.

     ~/Library/Group_Containers/group.com.apple.appleaccount.transparency/transparency.db
             The SQLite database used to persist transparency events for the
             current user.

SEE ALSO
     appleaccountd(8), launchd(8), launchd.plist(5)

